    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **283 tests, 0 failures**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `namesakeCount` feature, following the existing pattern used by fields like `membershipTier` and `customerCode`:\n\n1. **OpenAPI spec** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 added a read-only integer `namesakeCount` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **Domain model** (`Owner.java`) \u2014 added a `namesakeCount` field (`@Column(name = \"namesake_count\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n3. **Controller** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`) \u2014 added a `namesakeCount(owner)` helper that counts existing owners sharing the same last name (via `findAllOwners()`), computed and set just before the owner is saved \u2014 so it reflects the count \"at that moment\" and excludes the not-yet-persisted new owner. MapStruct maps it into the response automatically.\n\n4. **DB schemas** \u2014 added the `namesake_count` column to all four schema files (h2, hsqldb, postgres, mysql).\n\n5. **Test** \u2014 added `createOwnerReportsNamesakeCount`, which creates three owners with the same last name and asserts the response returns `0`, `1`, then `2`.\n\nThe V2 controller only lists owners (no creation), so no change was needed there.",
